From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmp: OLE control interfaces, persistence, FreezeEvents

Stubs (E_NOTIMPL / FIXME), as documented now.

- IOleObject: SetHostNames, Update and IsUpToDate are S_OK (not a linked
  object), GetUserClassID returns the control's CLSID, GetUserType, EnumVerbs
  and GetMiscStatus for aspects other than content are OLE_S_USEREG (the
  registry describes them), Advise / Unadvise / EnumAdvise go through an OLE
  advise holder (Unadvise and EnumAdvise are E_FAIL before any Advise).
  DoVerb now also handles OLEIVERB_SHOW, PRIMARY and UIACTIVATE: they
  activate in place, or just show the window when it is already there
  (E_UNEXPECTED without a client site). activate_inplace used the result of
  the previous query when the site only had IOleInPlaceSite.
  SetMoniker, GetMoniker, InitFromData, GetClipboardData and SetColorScheme
  stay E_NOTIMPL, as for any control that is not linkable.
- IOleInPlaceObjectWindowless: InPlaceDeactivate deactivates (tells the site,
  destroys the window), UIDeactivate is S_OK, ReactivateAndUndo is S_FALSE
  (nothing to undo), OnWindowMessage is S_FALSE (never windowless).
  ContextSensitiveHelp and GetDropTarget stay E_NOTIMPL.
- IOleControl: OnAmbientPropertyChange is S_OK, FreezeEvents counts and
  drops the events fired while frozen. GetControlInfo and OnMnemonic stay
  E_NOTIMPL (the control has no mnemonics).
- IProvideClassInfo2::GetGUID: E_POINTER, and GUID_NULL with E_INVALIDARG
  for a kind other than the default source interface.
- IPersistStreamInit: GetClassID, IsDirty (the persisted properties against
  the state at the last Load/Save/InitNew), Save, Load and GetSizeMax. The
  stream holds the persisted properties (autoStart, invokeURLs,
  enableErrorDialogs, mute, volume, balance, playCount, rate, modes, enabled,
  enableContextMenu, stretchToFit, windowlessVideo, uiMode, baseURL,
  defaultFrame and the URL) as a small versioned record; a stream that does
  not parse is E_FAIL and changes nothing.

